    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="0861" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1050: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Viborg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-19T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                                1919—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 165, December 15th. Department believes Viborg stores should be sent to
                    Reval at once for relief Yudenitch army and refugees or such other port as Gade
                    may deem best in view of possible Bolshevik advance.</p>
                <p>Your 167, 16th,<anchor n="82" xml:id="d866-f1"/> repeated to Gade.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
